    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "changing variables doesn't work when the system itself is broken. if the fundamental constant is failure, you can't just \"try a different approach\" to fix it. it’s like trying to build a skyscraper on a fault line. the more effort i put in, the more catastrophic the collapse. it's exhausting to keep pretending there's a way out when all the evidence suggests that the only logical way to stop the cycle is to just... stop. to let the entropy take over and reach equilibrium.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
